IMPORT prelude

-- Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (Western Australia) -- commencement (s 2) and the learner's permit transition
-- (s 66); the learner's permit (ss 10, 11A); when a driver's licence cannot be granted (ss 8, 9); loss of a provisional licence
-- (ss 16, 18); and the demerit points scheme of Part 4 (ss 40, 43-52) so far as a driver who is fined for speeding meets it.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47952, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47952.txt. The deposit names no compilation number. Its compilation table ends with the
-- Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Amendment (Driving Restrictions) Act 2024 (No. 45 of 2024, in force 16 November 2024); the
-- only reprint listed is Reprint 1 as at 3 July 2015; the uncommenced provisions table lists the Towing Services Act 2024 Pt 11
-- Div 4 (not shown, not encoded).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0008 (priority 1), raised 5 times by the three Western Australian cradle-to-grave lives:
-- Chloe c021 (2019-03-14, turns 16: "a learner's permit -- at what age, and with what conditions?") and c022 (2020-03-14, turns 17:
-- a provisional licence); Jake k032 (2023-08-30, turns 17: a provisional driver's licence) and k083 (2049-07-19, 25 km/h over on a
-- motorcycle: "an infringement and demerit points", Part 4); Daniel d012 (2012-10-15, turns 16: a learner's permit). The ledger
-- names "s 8 (learner's permit)", "provisional licence" and "Part 4 (demerit points)". SCOPED to those questions first, with the
-- definitions (s 3, s 40), conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 2 Division 3A (identity information); ss 4, 5A, 11-15 beyond what is said in comments (they are powers to
-- make regulations); Part 3 Division 2 and Division 3 (extraordinary licences); ss 53-60; Parts 5
-- and 6 other than s 66. The minimum age for a learner's permit, the age and conditions of a
-- provisional licence, the classes of licence, which offences are demerit point offences and how many points each carries are
-- all left by the Act to the regulations (ss 4, 10(5), 41); the regulations (named by c021 as the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Regulations 2014) were not
-- retrieved, so each of those is an INPUT and no figure from them appears here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 (WA) -- learners, provisional drivers and demerit points`

§§ `helpers`

-- Dates are given as year, month and day. A date's number orders dates (20190314 is 14 March 2019).
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`date number` MEANS `y` TIMES 10000 PLUS `m` TIMES 100 PLUS `d`

GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth month` IS A NUMBER, `birth day` IS A NUMBER, `on year` IS A NUMBER, `on month` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF `on month` GREATER THAN `birth month` OR (`on month` EQUALS `birth month` AND `on day` AT LEAST `birth day`)
    THEN `on year` MINUS `birth year`
    ELSE `on year` MINUS `birth year` MINUS 1

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- "At the end of a period of 3 years after the day on which ..." (s 10(4), s 48). The period begins the day after the starting day,
-- so it ends at the end of the third anniversary of that day. Something that lasts that long is still running on the anniversary
-- and gone the day after.
GIVEN `start year` IS A NUMBER, `start month` IS A NUMBER, `start day` IS A NUMBER, `on year` IS A NUMBER, `on month` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within 3 years after the day` IF
        `date number` `on year` `on month` `on day` AT LEAST `date number` `start year` `start month` `start day`
    AND `date number` `on year` `on month` `on day` AT MOST `date number` (`start year` PLUS 3) `start month` `start day`

§§ `2, 66 -- commencement and permits issued before it`

-- s 2: "(a) sections 1 and 2 -- on the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent; (b) the rest of the Act, on the day fixed
-- under the Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 section 2(b)." The compilation table: "Act other than s. 1 and 2: 27 Apr 2015
-- (see s. 2(b) and Gazette 17 Apr 2015 p. 1371)".
-- s 66: "A learner's permit issued to a person under the RT Act section 43(1) that was in effect immediately before commencement day
-- is, on and from commencement day, to be taken to be a learner's permit issued under section 10(1)." (RT Act = the Road Traffic Act
-- 1974 as in force before commencement day; commencement day here is also 27 April 2015 by note 2 of the compilation.)
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensing and demerit provisions are in operation on` IF
    `date number` `y` `m` `d` AT LEAST 20150427

GIVEN `issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 section 43(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `in effect immediately before 27 April 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old permit is taken to be a section 10 learner's permit` IF
    `issued under the Road Traffic Act 1974 section 43(1)` AND `in effect immediately before 27 April 2015`

§§ `10, 11A -- the learner's permit`

-- s 10(1): "The CEO may issue to a person a learner's permit authorising the person to drive a motor vehicle on a road solely for
-- the purpose of learning to drive it."
-- (2): "The permit does not authorise driving except in the course of driving instruction by -- (a) the holder of a licence issued
-- under the Motor Vehicle Drivers Instructors Act 1963; or (b) anyone else prescribed in the regulations."
-- (4): "The permit expires at the end of a period of 3 years after the day on which it is issued unless it has terminated before
-- then, and the CEO may cancel it at any time by notice in writing given to the permit holder."
-- (5): the regulations "may fix the minimum age below which, unless the CEO is satisfied that denial of the permit would occasion
-- undue hardship or inconvenience, a person cannot be issued with a learner's permit."
-- s 11A(2): the CEO "cannot issue a learner's permit until the applicant has provided ... any evidence required by the regulations to
-- establish the applicant's identity and residential address in this State"; (3) nor, except as prescribed or under (6), unless the
-- applicant has provided "a photograph taken at the time of the application" and "a signature made at the time of the application";
-- (6) or one provided under this Act or a related Act within the 10 years before.
-- The Act states no age. The minimum is an INPUT from the regulations. The CEO "may" issue: these rules say when the CEO cannot.
GIVEN `age of the applicant` IS A NUMBER, `minimum age fixed by the regulations` IS A NUMBER,
      `CEO satisfied denial would occasion undue hardship or inconvenience` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `identity and WA address evidence provided` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `photograph and signature provided at the application or within the previous 10 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the CEO is not barred from issuing a learner's permit` IF
        (    `age of the applicant` AT LEAST `minimum age fixed by the regulations`
         OR  `CEO satisfied denial would occasion undue hardship or inconvenience`)
    AND `identity and WA address evidence provided`
    AND `photograph and signature provided at the application or within the previous 10 years`

GIVEN `issued year` IS A NUMBER, `issued month` IS A NUMBER, `issued day` IS A NUMBER, `on year` IS A NUMBER, `on month` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER,
      `cancelled by the CEO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the learner's permit is in force` IF
        `within 3 years after the day` `issued year` `issued month` `issued day` `on year` `on month` `on day`
    AND (NOT `cancelled by the CEO`)

DECLARE Supervisor IS ONE OF
    `a licensed driving instructor`
    `a person prescribed in the regulations`
    `nobody`

GIVEN `permit in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `driving to learn` IS A BOOLEAN, `the supervisor` IS A Supervisor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the learner's permit authorises the driving` IF
        `permit in force`
    AND `driving to learn`
    AND CONSIDER `the supervisor`
        WHEN `nobody` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8, 9 -- when a driver's licence cannot be granted`

-- s 8(1): the CEO "cannot grant a driver's licence to a person unless -- (a) the CEO -- (i) is satisfied that the person usually
-- resides in this State; or (ii) is satisfied that the person does not usually reside in any other jurisdiction and does not hold,
-- and has never held, an Australian driver licence granted under the law of another jurisdiction; and (b) if the person has held --
-- (i) any Australian driver licence; or (ii) any licence ... granted ... by an external licensing authority, the person has ceased to
-- hold the licence or authorisation and has notified the CEO". (2): the CEO may in prescribed circumstances grant a licence to a
-- person who still holds an external (foreign) licence. (3): not a bar to an extraordinary licence. (4): "does not limit the
-- circumstances in which the CEO may refuse".
-- s 9(2): identity and WA address evidence; (3): "a photograph taken within 10 years of the application; and (b) a signature made
-- within 10 years", or one given under s 11A within the 10 years before (s 9(5)).
-- s 8 is the section the scenarios cite for the learner's permit. It is about residence and earlier licences, not age; and a
-- learner's permit is not a driver's licence (s 3: "driver's licence ... does not include a learner's permit").
GIVEN `usually resides in WA` IS A BOOLEAN, `usually resides in another jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds or has held another jurisdiction's licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `still holds an earlier Australian licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `still holds a foreign licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `a prescribed circumstance for keeping a foreign licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has held any Australian or foreign licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ceased earlier licences notified to the CEO` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `identity, address, photograph and signature provided` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an extraordinary licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the CEO is not barred from granting a driver's licence` IF
        `identity, address, photograph and signature provided`
    AND (    `an extraordinary licence`
         OR  (    (    `usually resides in WA`
                   OR  ((NOT `usually resides in another jurisdiction`) AND (NOT `holds or has held another jurisdiction's licence`)))
              AND (    (NOT `has held any Australian or foreign licence`)
                   OR  (    (NOT `still holds an earlier Australian licence`)
                        AND ((NOT `still holds a foreign licence`) OR `a prescribed circumstance for keeping a foreign licence`)
                        AND `ceased earlier licences notified to the CEO`))))

§§ `16, 18 -- losing a provisional licence`

-- s 3: "provisional licence means an Australian driver licence that specifies that it is a provisional licence". s 4(5)(c): the
-- regulations may "provide for the granting of a driver's licence as a provisional licence"; (5A) may impose restrictions on it.
-- Who gets a provisional licence, at what age and on what conditions is for the regulations: an INPUT.
-- s 16(1): if the holder of a provisional licence "(a) is convicted of an offence" in the list (Criminal Code s 277 arising from
-- driving, s 378 of a motor vehicle; Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 ss 32(4), 36, 44; Road Traffic Act 1974 ss 54, 55, 56, 61,
-- 62, 62A, 64AA, 64AC or 90, or prescribed) "or (b) is disqualified by a court ... the provisional licence is, by operation of this
-- subsection, cancelled." (2): the person is disqualified "for whichever of the following periods that terminates later -- (a) the
-- period for which the person is disqualified by the court; (b) a period of 3 months from the date of the person's conviction".
-- (3): "If the holder of a driver's licence that is a provisional licence is disqualified under Part 4 ... the provisional licence is,
-- by operation of this subsection, cancelled."
-- s 18: an unlicensed person who would get a provisional licence is disqualified the same way for the same offences, and also on
-- conviction under the Road Traffic Act 1974 s 49(1)(a).
DECLARE ProvisionalEvent IS ONE OF
    `convicted of an offence listed in section 16(1)`
    `disqualified by a court`
    `disqualified under Part 4`
    `disqualified by a fines enforcement licence suspension order`
    `an infringement notice paid without disqualification`

-- s 17: a fines enforcement licence suspension order (or a Road Traffic Act s 71C notice) SUSPENDS the provisional licence while the
-- disqualification lasts; it does not cancel it.
GIVEN `the event` IS A ProvisionalEvent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisional licence is cancelled by operation of law` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `convicted of an offence listed in section 16(1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disqualified by a court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disqualified under Part 4` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Reading: both periods are taken to run from the conviction, so the later-ending one is the longer one. If the court's period runs
-- from another day the comparison would be of end dates, which this does not model.
GIVEN `months disqualified by the court` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months of disqualification after a section 16 cancellation` MEANS `the greater of` `months disqualified by the court` 3

§§ `40 -- novice drivers`

-- s 40(2): "a person is a novice driver unless the person has, for a period of at least 2 years or periods adding up to at least 2
-- years, held -- (a) an Australian driver licence; or (b) a licence ... granted ... by an external licensing authority ... other than
-- solely for the purpose of learning". "novice driver (type 2) means a novice driver who has, for a period of at least 1 year or
-- periods adding up to at least 1 year, held" such a licence; "novice driver (type 1) means a novice driver who is not" type 2.
-- (3): periods when the person "was excluded by law from driving under that authorisation" do not count.
-- A learner's permit is not an Australian driver licence (s 3), so time on a permit does not count; a provisional licence does.
DECLARE NoviceStatus IS ONE OF
    `novice driver (type 1)`
    `novice driver (type 2)`
    `not a novice driver`

GIVEN `months held, not counting months excluded by law from driving` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NoviceStatus
`novice status` MEANS
    IF `months held, not counting months excluded by law from driving` AT LEAST 24
    THEN `not a novice driver`
    ELSE IF `months held, not counting months excluded by law from driving` AT LEAST 12
         THEN `novice driver (type 2)`
         ELSE `novice driver (type 1)`

§§ `43 -- the demerit point registry jurisdiction`

-- s 43(1): if a person holds a WA driver's licence or learner's permit, "this State is ... the demerit point registry jurisdiction";
-- (2): if the person holds another jurisdiction's driving authorisation, "that other jurisdiction"; (3): if neither but previously,
-- the jurisdiction of the authorisation previously held, or the most recent one; (4): "If this section does not otherwise identify
-- one, and only one, jurisdiction ... this State is" the registry jurisdiction.
-- So a person holding both a WA and an interstate authorisation is identified twice, and (4) makes WA the registry jurisdiction.
GIVEN `holds a WA licence or learner's permit` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds another jurisdiction's driving authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `previously held one` IS A BOOLEAN, `the most recent one was from WA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `WA is the demerit point registry jurisdiction` IF
        `holds a WA licence or learner's permit`
    OR  (    (NOT `holds another jurisdiction's driving authorisation`)
         AND ((NOT `previously held one`) OR `the most recent one was from WA`))

§§ `40(1A), 44, 45, 46 -- incurring demerit points`

-- s 40(1A): an alleged demerit point offence for which an infringement notice is issued "is dealt with by infringement notice -- ...
-- (b) if the Fines, Penalties and Infringement Notices Enforcement Act 1994 Part 3 applies ... the first time 1 of the following
-- events occurs -- (i) an amount is paid under the infringement notice (regardless of whether it is the full amount ...); (ii) an
-- order to pay or elect is issued ...; or (c) otherwise -- when an amount is paid". (1B): even a dishonoured payment counts.
-- (Paragraph (a), notices issued under another jurisdiction's law, turns on regulations and is not encoded.)
GIVEN `Fines Enforcement Act Part 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `any amount paid, even if dishonoured` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an order to pay or elect issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is dealt with by infringement notice` IF
        `any amount paid, even if dishonoured`
    OR  (`Fines Enforcement Act Part 3 applies` AND `an order to pay or elect issued`)

-- s 45: demerit point action "is to be taken" against a person for whom WA is the registry jurisdiction if dealt with by infringement
-- notice for a demerit point offence under a road law "or the law of another jurisdiction"; (2) against a person registered elsewhere
-- only for an offence "under a road law" (a WA offence). s 44: the same after a conviction, except (3) not where "because of the
-- conviction, the person was disqualified" -- and (4) disqualification for not paying the fine does not count.
-- s 46: "Demerit point action can be taken only against an individual." s 40, 41: what is a demerit point offence, and its points,
-- is prescribed by the regulations (an INPUT); s 41(2) "cannot be a demerit point offence in WA unless it involves the driving or use
-- of a motor vehicle".
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `dealt with by infringement notice`
    `convicted, not disqualified because of the conviction`
    `convicted and disqualified because of the conviction`
    `convicted and disqualified only for not paying the fine`
    `not yet dealt with`

GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `a prescribed demerit point offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `an offence under a WA road law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `WA is the registry jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN, `the outcome` IS AN Outcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `demerit point action is to be taken` IF
        `an individual`
    AND `a prescribed demerit point offence`
    AND (`WA is the registry jurisdiction` OR `an offence under a WA road law`)
    AND CONSIDER `the outcome`
        WHEN `convicted and disqualified because of the conviction` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `not yet dealt with` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `48 -- expiry`

-- s 48: "At the end of the period of 3 years after the day on which an offence was committed or allegedly committed, any demerit
-- points applying to the offence expire." The clock runs from the offence, not from payment or recording. s 40: "current demerit
-- points means demerit points that have been recorded ... and have not expired or been cancelled".
GIVEN `offence year` IS A NUMBER, `offence month` IS A NUMBER, `offence day` IS A NUMBER, `on year` IS A NUMBER, `on month` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER,
      `cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the points are current` IF
        `within 3 years after the day` `offence year` `offence month` `offence day` `on year` `on month` `on day`
    AND (NOT `cancelled`)

§§ `49 -- 12 or more points`

-- s 49(1): "If the number of current demerit points ... reaches at least 12, the CEO is to give the person ... an excessive demerit
-- points notice". (2): "(a) for less than 16 points, 3 months; (b) for at least 16 but less than 20 points, 4 months; (c) for at
-- least 20 points, 5 months", commencing "the 28th day after the notice is given or a later day". (3): points up to that day are
-- cancelled "whether or not the person makes a section 51 election". (4): disqualified if no election is made.
GIVEN `current demerit points` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months of disqualification in an excessive demerit points notice` MEANS
    IF `current demerit points` LESS THAN 12 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `current demerit points` LESS THAN 16 THEN 3
         ELSE IF `current demerit points` LESS THAN 20 THEN 4
              ELSE 5

§§ `50 -- novice drivers: 4 or 8 points`

-- s 50(2): "If the number of postcommencement demerit points ... reaches at least 4 in respect of any offence committed when the
-- person was a novice driver (type 1), or ... reaches at least 8 in respect of any offence committed when the person was a novice
-- driver (type 2), the CEO is to give the person, whether or not the person is still a novice driver, ... an excessive demerit points
-- (novice driver) notice"; (c) "the period of disqualification is 3 months"; (d) commencing "the day after the notice is given or a
-- later day". (4): disqualified for 3 months; no s 51 election is offered. (7): s 49 may also apply.
-- s 50(1) and note 1: postcommencement points exclude those for offences before 1 December 2010.
-- Reading: the count is of all the person's current postcommencement points, and the threshold is fixed by the novice type at the
-- time of the offence that takes the count there.
GIVEN `postcommencement current points after the offence` IS A NUMBER, `status when the offence was committed` IS A NoviceStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an excessive demerit points (novice driver) notice is due` IF
    CONSIDER `status when the offence was committed`
    WHEN `novice driver (type 1)` THEN `postcommencement current points after the offence` AT LEAST 4
    WHEN `novice driver (type 2)` THEN `postcommencement current points after the offence` AT LEAST 8
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `51, 52 -- the good behaviour election`

-- s 51(1): a person given an excessive demerit points notice "may ... avoid being disqualified ... by making an election ... for the
-- year". (2): "a person must hold a driver's licence other than a provisional licence and must not be a novice driver". (4): in
-- writing, "within 21 days after the day on which the CEO gave the excessive demerit points notice".
-- (3): the person elects not to commit in the year an offence, or offences, carrying "a total of 2 or more demerit points", or one
-- for which disqualification is mandatory or follows by operation of the Act.
-- s 52(1), (4): if 2 or more points are recorded for offences in the election period, or such a conviction follows, a notice
-- disqualifies the person for "double the period of disqualification that was stated in the excessive demerit points notice".
GIVEN `holds a driver's licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the licence is provisional` IS A BOOLEAN, `status` IS A NoviceStatus,
      `days after the notice was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 51 election may be made` IF
        `holds a driver's licence`
    AND (NOT `the licence is provisional`)
    AND `days after the notice was given` AT MOST 21
    AND CONSIDER `status`
        WHEN `not a novice driver` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `points recorded for offences in the election period` IS A NUMBER, `a conviction with mandatory or automatic disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the election is broken` IF
        `points recorded for offences in the election period` AT LEAST 2
    OR  `a conviction with mandatory or automatic disqualification`

GIVEN `months in the excessive demerit points notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months of disqualification after a broken election` MEANS `months in the excessive demerit points notice` TIMES 2
